# Problem Set 4 – Summary

## Part A – Permutations (Recursion)
* A recursive function to find all possible reorderings of a string.
* Base case: Single character string.
* Recursive step: Insert first character into all positions of the sub-problem permutations.

## Part B – Caesar Cipher (OOP)
* `Message` class: Basic string storage.
* `PlaintextMessage`: Handles encryption using a shift.
* `CiphertextMessage`: Decrypts by trying all 26 shifts and checking against a dictionary.
